   311	| Q | Ruling | Basis |
   312	| --- | --- | --- |
   313	| Q49a erasure commit in the journal (R-ERA-2, R-ERA-5) | An erasure commit is an ordinary data-journal transaction: it has a position, a txId, a record in `transactions()` and its own `:_tx/` facts, and its changes list only identities (entity, attribute, assertion ids), never values. It is also written to the erasure ledger kept apart from the data (TARGETS 7 item 5), which restore and rebuild replay. Earlier transactions' `:_tx/change` facts for erased values show the ErasedValue marker (modulo erasure), so the whole-journal comparison of ER-JOURNAL-MODULO compares markers on both sides. | TARGETS 7; Q24, Q31f |
   314	| Q49b idempotence (R-ERA-3) | Accepted: the first erasure of an identity sets `erasedAt`; erasing it again changes nothing; an erase that matches nothing still commits (a journal record with an empty change list). | idempotent commands |
   315	| Q49c erased values in queries (R-ERA-4; provisional, under the Q24 flag for Sam) | An erased value is present with no readable value: it matches no value predicate (equality, inequality, range, pattern), so a filter never selects or rejects a subject by it; value aggregates (SUM, AVG, MIN, MAX) skip it while COUNT of assertions counts it; ORDER BY places erased markers last in a deterministic order by assertion id; grouping puts all erased values of an attribute in one group keyed by the marker; Unique ignores erased values; an erased reference cannot be followed (an include returns the marker). | hard error, never silent; deterministic answers |
   316	| Q49d in-flight reads (R-ERA-6) | Accepted: for a read that started before the erasure published, each erased value may be the old value or the marker. | TARGETS 7 item 1 |
   317	| Q49e JSON number to decimal (R-DEC-18) | A JSON number converts from its as-written reading (Q33a's read-back-as-written text): toDecimal(json 0.1, 2, 1) = 0.1. The exact binary64 expansion is never used for JSON. Decimal text inside a JSON string is E-INVALID-VALUE unless the query converts the string explicitly. | Q33a |
