   596	### 4.5 Cardinality-many order
   597	
   598	set semantics: equal values collapse to one element; elements ordered first by type family, then by value. Family order: boolean, integer, number, decimal, datetime, string, ref, json, blob. boolean: false < true; integer: numeric; number: numeric IEEE (-0.0 and +0.0 collapse, CMP-NEGZERO); decimal: exact numeric value (1.50 and 1.5 are one value); datetime: instant; string: Unicode codepoint sequence; ref: codepoint sequence of the target id; json: codepoint sequence of the canonical JSON text; blob: codepoint sequence of the content id. Family order per RULINGS Q14a and Q18: decimal is its own family between number and datetime; inside it, values sort by exact numeric value.
