  1094	
  1095	### 7.2 Numbers (CS-NUMERIC) and errors (CS-ERRORS)
  1096	
  1097	Every example in sections 4.1 to 4.4 is a CS-NUMERIC case with that expected answer. CS-ERRORS has one case per ERROR_TABLE entry reachable from a read surface.
  1098	
  1099	### 7.3 Fault points (CS-FAULT)
  1100	
  1101	The expected outcome after a fault is chosen from the last transition with durable or engine-side evidence observed by the fault injector after the crash (the log file's records read back, the engine's committed transactions, the publication marker), never from the system's own claim. A transition the protocol declares but the receipt does not witness fails the case.
  1102	
  1103	**qlever transitions.**
  1104	
  1105	| Transition | Witness evidence |
  1106	| --- | --- |
  1107	| QT0-RECEIVED | broker request log entry |
  1108	| QT1-VALIDATED | group member accepted against staged state (broker trace) |
  1109	| QT2-LOGGED | COMMIT record present in the log file after restart (fsync completed); this is the irrevocable decision |
  1110	| QT3-APPLY-SENT | update operation sent (broker trace) |
  1111	| QT4-PUBLISHED | publication marker for the group's P visible in a query |
  1112	| QT5-VERIFIED | complete expected effects and absences checked (broker trace and independent query through three access paths) |
  1113	| QT6-ACKED | caller received the success receipt |
  1114	
  1115	**qlever expected outcomes.**
  1116	
  1117	| Fault after | Final state | Original caller | Retry with the same commandId | Reads |
  1118	| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  1119	| QT0-RECEIVED or QT1-VALIDATED (no QT2 evidence) | the command is absent unless a later attempt commits it; it is never committed twice | typed failure or E-OUTCOME-UNKNOWN; never success | evaluated as a fresh command (commits at most once in total) | - |
  1120	| QT2-LOGGED (no QT4 evidence) | the group MUST be published by recovery with the position decided at QT2; it can never become absent | E-OUTCOME-UNKNOWN or E-COMMIT-PENDING; never success before publication | before publication: E-COMMIT-PENDING or E-REPAIRING; after publication: the original success receipt (same txId and position) | never show the group before publication; E-REPAIRING while fenced |
  1121	| QT3-APPLY-SENT (no QT4 evidence) | as QT2-LOGGED; partial permutation state must not be served: the lane fences and recovery re-applies or rebuilds | as QT2-LOGGED | as QT2-LOGGED | E-REPAIRING while fenced; after recovery all access paths agree |
  1122	| QT4-PUBLISHED (no QT5 evidence) | published; recovery completes verification before any new write | E-OUTCOME-UNKNOWN or success; success only if publication was established | the original success receipt once publication is established, else E-REPAIRING | may show the group; E-REPAIRING while fenced |
  1123	| QT5-VERIFIED failure (verification mismatch) | lane fenced; recovery republishes the logged state; final state equals O-REPLAY with the group present | no success until recovery establishes publication | E-REPAIRING until recovered, then the original success receipt | E-REPAIRING while fenced |
  1124	| QT5-VERIFIED (no QT6 evidence): lost ACK | published | E-OUTCOME-UNKNOWN | the original success receipt | show the group |
  1125	
  1126	A success receipt is valid only if its timestamp is after the group's QT4-PUBLISHED evidence; a read by the same client issued after the success receipt sees the group (read-your-writes).
  1127	
  1128	**xtdb transitions.**
  2700	
  2701	**`R.evaluator.incomplete-receipts`: Incomplete receipts cannot close an obligation.**
  2702	- Statement: The evaluator ships every EVALUATOR_COUNTEREXAMPLES receipt set and judges each OPEN, and every EVALUATOR_POSITIVE_FIXTURES receipt set and judges each CLOSED (O-CONTRACT); both catalogs cover every closure rule any obligation uses, so an evaluator that always answers OPEN, or always CLOSED, fails (RULINGS Q26, Q31k).
  2703	- Lanes: all three; receipt scope engine. Verifier mode: rerun.
  2704	- Cases: CS-EVAL-COUNTER (all, COMPILED); CS-EVAL-COUNTER (CX-CALIBRATION-EMPTY, CX-CALIBRATION-MISSING, CX-NS-MISSING-BAR, CX-NS-FEWER-RUNS, CX-NS-ECHOED-BASIS, CX-NS-UNFROZEN-TRACE, CX-GS-WRONG-SCENARIO, CX-GS-NO-WITNESSES, CX-SELECTION-SHORT, CX-ZERO-MODES, CX-COUNTEREXAMPLE-EDITED, CX-MUTANT-NO-REACH, CX-MUTANT-CRASH-KILL, CX-OBS-COVERAGE-GAP, CX-FAULT-REPS-SHORT, CX-STATIC-EXTRA, CX-SCALE-COUNT, CX-METRIC-MISSING, CX-REQ-NO-STATEMENT, CX-MATRIX-NO-EXCEPTION, CX-PROVENANCE-INPUT, CX-WITNESS-CLIENT-COUNTERS, CX-BUDGET-UNFROZEN, CX-SCREENING, CX-STALE-DEFINITION, CX-COMPOSITION-UNBOUND, CX-NO-VERIFIER, CX-W0-UNPINNED, CX-W0-FLOOR-MISSED, CX-P2-REJECTS-VALID, CX-FORGED-DENSITY, CX-CLAIM-NULL-ORACLE-PIN, CX-CLAIM-SUPPLIED-NAMES, CX-XTDB-SHARED-LANGUAGE, CX-SCREENING-CLAIM-PREREQ, CX-ZERO-OBJECT-HASHES, CX-STALE-BINARY, CX-EARLIER-COMMIT-FALSIFIER, CX-NO-MEASUREMENT, CX-UNKNOWN-OBLIGATION, CX-REFUSAL-AS-AUTHORING, CX-POSITION-GATE, CX-R6-UNOPENED-MEANING, CX-R6-UNMATCHED-CONTROL, CX-R6-INDIRECT-REFUSAL, PX-PASS-ALL, PX-COUNTEREXAMPLE, PX-MUTANT-KILL, PX-OBSERVE, PX-FAULT, PX-STATIC, PX-SCALE, PX-METRICS, PX-NS, PX-GS, PX-REQUIREMENT, PX-CALIBRATION, PX-MATRIX, PX-PROVENANCE, PX-WITNESS, PX-BUDGET, PX-W0-COVERAGE, COMPILED).
