  2711	
  2712	### NS. North star: Sam's five priorities P1 to P5 on the fixed writer trace
  2713	
  2714	**`NS.P1`: P1: many concurrent pinned reads that never block writers (per surface).**
  2715	- Statement: With the frozen writer trace running, closed-loop readers at 1, 4, 16, 64 and 256 (and 1,024 stress) each name their basis (valid time and record time or tx), in the lane's language, under TARGETS 1.1 P1: readers and writers share one hot set (at least half the reads target subjects written in the previous 60 s, NS-P1-HOT-SET); 10% of subgraph reads are split into two or more queries at the same named basis, scheduled to straddle a command the frozen trace already holds for that subject (step 1 before its ACK, step 2 after), and must equal the oracle at the requested basis (NS-P1-SPLIT-READ); the driver adds no writes of its own, so faster readers never change the write load (NS-P1-SPLIT-NO-DRIVER-WRITES, RULINGS Q31b); every window contains at least one maintenance event (NS-P1-MAINTENANCE-IN-WINDOW); the driver records the requested basis itself and the verifier checks answers at it (NS-P1-DRIVER-BASIS); reader-caused writer waits are attributed by matched-phase comparison against the zero-reader run and by engine-side wait evidence where the engine exposes it (NS-P1-WAIT-ATTRIBUTION). Every NS-P1-* bar holds: zero violations, goodput at 256 not below 64, read p99 within NS-P1-READ-P99-256-MS, writer commit p99 within NS-P1-WRITER-P99-RATIO-256 of its zero-reader baseline, no command waits beyond NS-P1-WRITER-WAIT-MAX-MS, and at 1,024 goodput within NS-P1-GOODPUT-1024-VS-256, writer p99 within NS-P1-WRITER-P99-RATIO-1024, back to the 256-level bar within NS-P1-RECOVERY-MS.
  2716	- Lanes: all three; receipt scope lane. Verifier mode: re-evaluate-and-spot.
  2717	- Cases: CS-NS (p1-ladder, p1-stress, COMPILED); CS-NS (NS-P1-HOT-SET, NS-P1-SPLIT-READ, NS-P1-SPLIT-NO-DRIVER-WRITES, NS-P1-MAINTENANCE-IN-WINDOW, NS-P1-DRIVER-BASIS, NS-P1-WAIT-ATTRIBUTION, COMPILED).
  2718	- Oracles: O-REPLAY (BUILT-ACCEPTED), O-OBS (TO-BUILD). Entrypoints: EP-REPO, EP-NATIVE, EP-WRITER, EP-ENGINE-OBS. Profiles: P-YEAR-ONE, P-NS.
  2719	- Closure: CR-NS; modes single-execution; thresholds NS-P1-VIOLATIONS-MAX, NS-P1-GOODPUT-256-VS-64, NS-P1-READ-P99-256-MS, NS-P1-WRITER-P99-RATIO-256, NS-P1-WRITER-WAIT-MAX-MS, NS-P1-GOODPUT-1024-VS-256, NS-P1-WRITER-P99-RATIO-1024, NS-P1-RECOVERY-MS, T-RUNS; params {"gates": ["GATE-POSITION", "GATE-ORACLE-PIN"]}.
  2720	- Sources: lab/NORTH-STAR.md; lab/TARGETS.md sections 1 and 2.
  2721	- Status: OPEN.
  2722	
  2723	**`NS.P2`: P2: small, atomic, idempotent per-subject commits with low latency.**
  2724	- Statement: Open loop under TARGETS 1.1 P2: commands are offered on the frozen schedule and latency runs from the scheduled offer to the published ACK (sent only once the commit is durable and readable), so queueing behind other writers counts. The trace's own commands are reported per size band: the 5-to-10 band (NS-P2-BAND-5-10) and the 11-to-25 band (NS-P2-BAND-11-25) each meet NS-P2-COMMIT-P50-MS and NS-P2-COMMIT-P99-MS, the 26-to-50 band (NS-P2-BAND-26-50) meets NS-P2-COMMIT-P99-26-50-MS, all with P1's 256 readers running; the 10-fact probe is a diagnostic only. Every offered command is committed with a receipt, rejected with a typed error, or a typed conflict (NS-P2-UNACCOUNTED-MAX, NS-P2-ACCOUNTING), and accounting is not progress: every oracle-valid trace command publishes; typed rejections count only for the trace's deliberately invalid commands and typed conflicts only where the oracle independently finds a compare-and-set race (NS-P2-UNJUSTIFIED-OUTCOMES-MAX, NS-P2-PROGRESS); queued commands never exceed NS-P2-QUEUE-MAX-S of the offered rate at steady state (NS-P2-QUEUE-BOUND) and the queue drains within NS-P2-BURST-DRAIN-S after each burst (NS-P2-BURST-DRAIN) (RULINGS Q31a). The pull at the returned tx sees the commit every time with no extra wait (NS-P2-RYOW-FRACTION); duplicates and lost ACKs return the original receipt every time (NS-P2-DUP-RECEIPT-FRACTION).
  2725	- Lanes: all three; receipt scope engine. Verifier mode: re-evaluate-and-spot.

