  1327	| watermarkRouting | a read that finds no eligible index waits at most T-WATERMARK-WAIT-MS for one, then routes to an eligible fallback (the source of truth's own query surface or another index); the fallback's latency counts in the read's own latency; the receipt records the route and the surface language, a cross-language fallback is counted per surface, and fallbacks are reported as a share of reads per window; no index answers for a basis it is not eligible for (RULINGS Q31d) |
  1328	| fallbackEquivalence | outage read-your-own-write is tested on every serving surface the composition claims, native surfaces included; a stale fallback is rejected; where a fallback answers in another language, both recipes are bound to one semantic query identity (parameters, basis, meaning) and one expected answer from the oracle; total request latency and language attribution stay recorded (RULINGS Q34b) |
