2211:**`G7.composition.ack-and-routed-ryow`: ACK after source publication; read-your-own-write by routing.**
2212:- Statement: Per COMPOSITION ackOwnership (RULINGS Q31e, replacing Q28's ACK clause): the source of truth sends every ACK after its own publication (CO-ACK-AFTER-SOURCE-PUBLICATION, OBS-ACK-ORDER); the pull at the returned position is served by an index eligible for it, else by the fallback, so read-your-own-write is exact (CO-RYOW-ROUTED); during a current-index outage commits and ACKs continue and pulls fall back (CO-OUTAGE-ACKS-CONTINUE), and the index catches up from the feed through a bounded queue (CO-CATCHUP-BOUNDED-QUEUE). Per COMPOSITION fallbackEquivalence (RULINGS Q34b), this holds on every serving surface the composition claims in the lane's language, native included (CO-RYOW-PER-SURFACE); a stale fallback is rejected (CO-STALE-FALLBACK-REJECTED); a cross-language fallback recipe is bound to the same semantic query identity (parameters, basis, meaning) and the same oracle answer (CO-CROSS-LANGUAGE-RECIPE-IDENTITY), with total request latency and language attribution recorded.
2325:**`G8.composition.watermark-routing`: Reads are served only by an index eligible for their basis.**
2326:- Statement: Per COMPOSITION eligibility (RULINGS Q31d): an index serves basis B only when its watermark, a fully resolved prefix, has reached B in B's epoch (CO-EPOCH-MISMATCH), C1's conditions hold, it can reconstruct B (a current-only index only inside the validity interval of every attribute read, CO-RECONSTRUCT-OUTSIDE-VALIDITY) and it has applied every published erasure (CO-ERASURE-FRONTIER); a read with no eligible index waits at most T-WATERMARK-WAIT-MS (CO-WATERMARK-WAIT) and then routes to an eligible fallback (CO-WATERMARK-FALLBACK) whose latency counts in the read's own latency (CO-FALLBACK-LATENCY-COUNTS); the receipt records the route and the surface language, a cross-language fallback is counted per surface (CO-FALLBACK-LANGUAGE), and fallbacks are reported as a share of reads per window (CO-FALLBACK-SHARE, OBS-WATERMARK); no index answers for a basis it is not eligible for (CO-NO-STALE-ANSWER); history and analytics trail asynchronously behind their watermarks (CO-ASYNC-HISTORY).
2623:**`G10.composition.identity-bound`: Receipts bind the whole composition.**
2723:**`NS.P2`: P2: small, atomic, idempotent per-subject commits with low latency.**
2732:**`NS.P3`: P3: an ordered, resumable change feed.**
